# Pack 4: rak-shor v1 failed the disc_overflow gate (max opaque radius 0.987 > 0.867): the tall bone-crook staff (and its skull head) stood far above the head and crossed the disc rim. Same design and identity, drawn smaller with a short staff held close to the body.
RK_FIT = " Calibration from the previous generation of this exact token: the design was right, but the tall bone-crook staff with its skull-and-crescent head towered far above the figure and crossed the outer rim of the disc. This time keep the same upright old green orc in black-and-violet robes with the spiked collar and bone shoulder pauldrons, but draw the WHOLE figure clearly smaller and the staff SHORT: the bone staff is gripped near its middle at his side and its crook head ends no higher than his own head, well inside the disc, at least a sixth of the disc radius away from the disc edge and never in the upper-right or upper-left corners. Every part of him, the staff head included, sits inside a circle of about two thirds of the disc radius."
retry('rak-shor', 4, comp=COMP + FIT + COMPACT + RK_FIT)

# Pack 5: warmaster-gnarg v1 failed only the base_drift gate (median -9.24, tolerance +-8; radius 0.860 and occupancy passed): the disc came out darker than the reference, mostly on the left and lower side (sector offsets down to -15.9), under the sword and the dark armour. Same design, disc kept at reference lightness all round with no shadow of the armour or sword on it, and the armour a lighter steel value.
GN_DISC = " Calibration from the previous generation of this exact token: the design was right, but the base disc came out clearly DARKER than the style reference, especially along the left and lower left rim and under the sword and legs. This time keep the same braced horizontal-greatsword orc warlord in violet-steel plate, spiked pauldrons and crimson cloak, but render the WHOLE disc, its outer ring band and the plate under the figure, at the style reference's own lightness or a hair lighter, evenly all round, with NO cast shadow, dark contact shadow or ambient darkening of the disc from the armour, the sword or the legs. Make the plate armour a lighter mid-value violet-steel with broad pale lavender-grey highlight planes so the figure does not read as a dark mass on the disc."
retry('warmaster-gnarg', 5, comp=COMP + FIT + COMPACT + GN_DISC)

# Pack 6: orc-assassin v1 passed the gate (drift -3.84, radius 0.860) but is dark: masked-body luminance 48.4 (floor 45, the 9th darkest of 252 tokens) and at 48px the near-black navy hood and jerkin merge into a dark blob with the charcoal disc. Same crouched two-dagger pose and identity, a clearly lighter slate-blue leather and brighter skin.
AS_BRIGHT = " Calibration from the previous generation of this exact token: it passed the gate, but at 48px the near-black navy hood, jerkin and boots merged into one dark blob on the charcoal disc. This time keep the same very low stalking crouch with a dagger in each hand in reverse grip and the masked hooded head, but make the leather clearly LIGHTER: a mid-value slate-blue-grey leather (a light steel-blue on the lit upper-left planes, broad pale highlight planes on the hood, shoulders and knees, pale cream stitching and belts), brighter warm olive-green skin on the forearms and hands, a pale steel dagger blades and bright yellow eyes, so the whole figure is a mid-light value shape well above the disc value with a bright edge on its upper-left side. Never near-black anywhere except the eye slits."
retry('orc-assassin', 6, comp=COMP + FIT + COMPACT + AS_BRIGHT)

