DOG_BRIGHT = " Calibration from the previous generation of this exact token: it passed the gate, but at 48px the near-black fur merged into one dark blob on the charcoal disc. This time draw the corrupted war dog SIDE-ON in a snarling lunging stance, seen from the side and slightly above, head turned toward the viewer with the jaws WIDE OPEN showing pale teeth, front legs and hind legs clearly separated from the body with daylight between them, the head clearly separate from the shoulders. Make the coat a MID charcoal-grey, clearly LIGHTER than the disc, with broad pale ash-grey highlight planes on the back, shoulders and haunches, a PALE BONE-WHITE ash underbelly, chest and muzzle, a studded iron collar with a short broken chain, and BRIGHT violet and acid-green glowing corruption veins and cracks across the ribs, shoulders and face, glowing green eyes. Distinct from the shipped brown dire wolf: grey not brown, spiked collar, open jaws, glowing veins. Never near-black anywhere except the mouth interior."
retry('corrupted-war-dog', 7, comp=COMP + FIT + COMPACT + DOG_BRIGHT)

